l users, orders, `user_id` references, and historical `created_at`.\n  - Applies deterministic cleanup:\n    - `u4` → `ada+u4@example.com`\n    - `u5` → `missing+u5@example.invalid`\n    - `u6` → `missing+u6@example.invalid`\n  - Adds `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n  - Enforces `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE`.\n  - Safe to execute twice without duplicating rows.\n\n- `preflight_report.md`\n  - Documents duplicate, null, and blank email issues.\n  - Documents dependent orders for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`.\n\n- `rollback.sql`\n  - Restores the pre-migration `users` shape: `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n  - Preserves users and orders.\n  - Documents that original dirty email values cannot be reconstructed.\n\n- `postcheck.sql`\n  - Verifies row counts, order references, cleaned emails, null/blank values, duplicates, status values, and schema declarations.\n\n- `migration_report.md`\n  - Summarizes strategy, cleanup, idempotency, rollback behavior, and postchecks.\n\nVerification completed with Python’s built-in SQLite engine:\n\n- Migration produced 6 users and 4 orders.\n- Dirty emails were cleaned exactly as required.\n- All dependent order references remained unchanged.\n- Re-running migration preserved 6 users and 4 orders.\n- Rollback restored columns `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n- Rollback preserved all rows and passed `PRAGMA foreign_key_check`.\n- Existing `schema.sql` and `migration_policy.md` were not edited.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0c7af19cfa8a603f016a951ff3734c87d28a54370641992aee\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":437,"output":389,"cacheRead":28416,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29242,"cost":{"input":0.00008740000000000001,"output":0.00046679999999999996,"cacheRead":0.00056832,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00112252}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1788157938786,"responseId":"resp_0c7af19cfa8a603f016a951ff3191087d29debf7300e291110","d